From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:43:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Stop the callback threads before what they use goes away

Each client has a thread that delivers the callbacks to the application.
CLibCEC's destructor cleared its list of clients and deleted the processor
while those threads still ran: a command still queued is logged through
the processor (CCECClient::AddCommand()) and every log line goes through
the list of clients (CLibCEC::AddLog()). Destroying libCEC while commands
from the TV were still queued read the list while it was cleared, and the
processor after it was deleted.

CCECClient::StopCallbacks() stops that thread once the callback it is in
returns, and the destructor calls it for each client before it clears the
list and deletes the processor. Callbacks still queued at that point are
not delivered, as when a client was deleted before.

Idea: pannal (CoreELEC), who stops the callback workers before the
processor is retired.

Tests (outside the tree): libCEC built on the host with AddressSanitizer
and ThreadSanitizer; 200 instances destroyed with commands queued for the
application (a heap buffer overflow in CLibCEC::AddLog() before, none
after).
---
 src/libcec/CECClient.cpp | 5 +++++
 src/libcec/CECClient.h   | 6 ++++++
 src/libcec/LibCEC.cpp    | 5 +++++
 3 files changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/libcec/CECClient.cpp b/src/libcec/CECClient.cpp
index b779c18..98f3748 100644
--- a/src/libcec/CECClient.cpp
+++ b/src/libcec/CECClient.cpp
@@ -1831,6 +1831,11 @@ int CCECClient::QueueCommandHandler(const cec_command& command)
   return result;
 }
 
+void CCECClient::StopCallbacks(void)
+{
+  StopThread(0);
+}
+
 void* CCECClient::Process(void)
 {
   CCallbackWrap* cb(NULL);
diff --git a/src/libcec/CECClient.h b/src/libcec/CECClient.h
index a9cc4a7..4a0d6b3 100644
--- a/src/libcec/CECClient.h
+++ b/src/libcec/CECClient.h
@@ -363,6 +363,12 @@ namespace CEC
     void QueueSourceActivated(bool bActivated, const cec_logical_address logicalAddress);
     int QueueCommandHandler(const cec_command& command);
 
+    /*!
+     * @brief Stop the thread that calls the application, once the callback that it is in returns.
+     * Callbacks that are still queued are not delivered, as when the client is deleted.
+     */
+    void StopCallbacks(void);
+
     // callbacks
     virtual void                  Alert(const libcec_alert type, const libcec_parameter &param) { QueueAlert(type, param); }
     virtual void                  AddLog(const cec_log_message_cpp &message) { QueueAddLog(message); }
diff --git a/src/libcec/LibCEC.cpp b/src/libcec/LibCEC.cpp
index f5114cb..736ae8f 100644
--- a/src/libcec/LibCEC.cpp
+++ b/src/libcec/LibCEC.cpp
@@ -63,6 +63,11 @@ CLibCEC::~CLibCEC(void)
   if (m_cec && m_cec->IsRunning())
     m_cec->UnregisterClients();
 
+  // stop the threads that call the application before what those calls go through goes away:
+  // the list of clients, which every log line is sent to, and the processor
+  for (std::vector<CECClientPtr>::iterator it = m_clients.begin(); it != m_clients.end(); it++)
+    (*it)->StopCallbacks();
+
   m_clients.clear();
 
   // delete the adapter connection
